<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | BarcodeNest" description="How BarcodeNest handles account, authentication, and API usage information.">
  <article class="narrow legal">
    <div class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</div><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p><strong>Last updated: November 25, 2026</strong></p>
    <h2>Registration</h2><p>Registration collects your name and email address. If you continue with Google or GitHub, we also store the provider name and its durable account identifier so future sign-ins reach the correct BarcodeNest account. To enforce the one-Free-account policy, we store a one-way keyed hash of the registration network address while the account exists; the raw address is not stored in this registration record. We use this information to create and administer API access, provide support, enforce quotas, and protect the service from abuse.</p>
    <h2>Authentication</h2><p>Passwords are stored as one-way Argon2id hashes. OAuth-only accounts do not have a BarcodeNest password. Account-session records support login, token rotation, security monitoring, and logout; raw passwords are never stored.</p>
    <h2>API access</h2><p>Operational records include API-key identifiers, request counts, quota usage, and security logs needed to provide and protect the service. Raw API keys are shown once; BarcodeNest stores a cryptographic digest rather than the raw key.</p>
    <h2>Private Vault records</h2><p>When you save a product, we store the identifier and the names, prices, categories, image links, notes and custom fields you provide to maintain your private workspace. These records are restricted to your account and are not automatically added to the public product catalog. You can edit or delete them in My Barcode Vault. Saving a linked image stores its URL; the Vault does not download or store the image file. For account deletion or a personal-data access request, contact support.</p><h2>Workspace records and operational history</h2><p>Catalogue variants, identifiers, label templates, uploaded template logos, inventory balances and stock movements, and asset assignments and maintenance history are private to your account. Keep personnel details limited to what you need. Inventory and asset histories are retained to support an auditable register; records with stock history cannot be deleted through the product form, and zero-stock inventory can be archived. Contact support for account deletion or data access.</p><h2>First-party usage analytics</h2><p>We collect an allowlisted event name, tool category and timestamp to understand tool use and conversion. A random identifier stored in the current browser tab links anonymous visits to account activity after sign-in. The server stores its hash and an internal account identifier for authenticated events. These events do not include product records, barcode values, API keys, file contents, names, email addresses, IP addresses or user-agent strings, and are not sent to third-party analytics services. Browser events respect Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control. Registration and billing activation counters are recorded by the server. A bounded retention task removes event rows older than 90 days, with cleanup retried every six hours; a backlog or outage may delay deletion.</p><h2>Product data</h2><p>Initial grocery data is derived from Open Food Facts. BarcodeNest provides an indexed API service layer and does not claim ownership of Open Food Facts data.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2><p>For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:support@barcodenest.com"><u>support@barcodenest.com</u></a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
